language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Print a set of templates, each with n_slots slots, to produce the demanded number of copies of every variation, minimising the number of printed sheets.
given n_slots, n_templates, n_var : int
given demand : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_var)] of int(0..10000)
find layout : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates), int(1..n_var)] of int(0..n_slots)
find production : matrix indexed by [int(1..n_templates)] of int(0..max(demand))

branching on [layout, production]

minimising (sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t])
such that
$ each template has n_slots printing slots, so it carries at most n_slots variations
forAll t : int(1..n_templates) . ((sum j : int(1..n_var) . layout[t,j]) <= n_slots),
$ every variation's demand is met: the copies printed over all sheets cover the demand (overprinting allowed)
forAll j : int(1..n_var) . ((sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t] * layout[t,j]) >= demand[j]),
$ the templates are interchangeable, so they are listed by non-increasing number of sheets to break symmetry
forAll t : int(1..n_templates-1) . (production[t] >= production[t+1]),
$ every sheet prints at most n_slots copies, so the sheets printed must cover the total demand
((sum t : int(1..n_templates) . production[t]) * n_slots) >= (sum j : int(1..n_var) . demand[j])
